+# Local VS Code development, Kaggle GPU execution
+
+PR #12 is based on `multibranch/v0/develop`. Keep working on that branch and
+`notebooks/multibranch_attention.ipynb`, with Python modules in `src/`.
+The similarly named `multi_branch/develop` is a different branch.
+
+## Install these additions on Windows
+
+Copy the files in this setup archive into your existing project root. The archive
+contains additions and a patch; it does not replace your notebook or utility files.
+Append `gitignore-additions.txt` to your existing `.gitignore`. Alternatively,
+apply only `cmi_kaggle_setup.patch` with `git apply` on the PR #12 branch instead
+of copying the additions. Do not use both installation methods.
+In PowerShell:
+
+```powershell
+Set-Location 'C:\Users\maran\OneDrive\Documents\Git Profile\cmi_dexter'
+git branch --show-current
+python -m pip install -r requirements-kaggle.txt
+python scripts/kaggle_experiment.py auth
+```
+
+Choose your intended Python environment in VS Code first. The tasks use that
+interpreter. CLI-only submission does not require a local TensorFlow/GPU install.
+For running the notebook locally, your existing ML environment is still required.
+This script requires Python 3.10 or newer.
+
+Sign in as `keithmarange` using Kaggle's browser authentication flow. Alternatively,
+generate an API token in https://www.kaggle.com/settings/api and save it in
+`C:\Users\maran\.kaggle\access_token`. Existing legacy credentials in
+`C:\Users\maran\.kaggle\kaggle.json` are also supported by the CLI.
+Never put credentials in the repository or notebook.
+
+Accept the competition rules while signed in at
+https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/cmi-detect-behavior-with-sensor-data/rules .
+Ensure your Kaggle account has GPU access and remaining quota.
+
+## Daily workflow
+
+Save the notebook and changed modules in VS Code, then run:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/kaggle_experiment.py prepare
+python scripts/kaggle_experiment.py push
+python scripts/kaggle_experiment.py status
+# Run once the job reports COMPLETE:
+python scripts/kaggle_experiment.py download
+```
+
+The same commands are available under Terminal > Run Task > Kaggle in VS Code.
+`prepare` is optional before `push`: pushing always rebuilds from saved local files.
+`push` creates a new executable version of `keithmarange/multibranch-attention`.
+The metadata requests a private GPU notebook with internet access and attached
+CMI competition data. Inspect/edit `kaggle/kernel-metadata.json` if you want another
+kernel ID or visibility. This executes the existing full search, including its
+37 Bayesian iterations; it may consume substantial GPU time.
+
+Generated submission files live in `kaggle_build/multibranch_attention/`.
+An added first cell reconstructs the current `src/*.py` files in
+`/kaggle/working/src`, installs missing scikit-optimize/PyWavelets, checks TensorFlow
+GPU access and locates competition data. It preserves Kaggle's TensorFlow install.
+The original experiment cells and parameter spaces are unchanged.
+Working-directory routing places the notebook's existing result directories under
+`/kaggle/working`, where Kaggle retains outputs.
+
+Downloads go to `results/kaggle/<download-time>/<original-output-path>/` and include:
+
+- `multibranch_attention_cv.csv`
+- `multibranch_attention_best.csv` (best parameters and scores)
+- `multibranch_attention_holdout.csv`
+
+The downloader requests those CSVs, avoiding the large saved H5 model. It requires
+a complete set and uses fresh download folders to avoid stale outputs. Check status
+before downloading; a failed job will not yield a complete result set. The included
+`local_submission.json` records the last locally prepared source hashes and branch;
+it is local provenance, not a server-confirmed version association. Avoid concurrent
+submissions from multiple machines to the same kernel ID.
+
+To inspect the existing remote notebook without overwriting local work:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/kaggle_experiment.py pull
+```
+
+This implements `kaggle kernels pull keithmarange/multibranch-attention -m` into
+`kaggle_build/multibranch_attention/remote/`. Do not pull into `notebooks/` while
+editing, because that may overwrite local work.
+
+## Validation and current limits
+
+```powershell
+python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+Offline packaging and result-collection integration tests pass. They verify that
+the submitted experiment cells are identical, embedded module bytes match `src/`,
+nested CSV output is collected, and incomplete/unsafe archives are rejected.
+The existing parameter contract tests also pass; TensorFlow construction tests were
+skipped in the setup session because TensorFlow was unavailable.
+
+Kaggle CLI 2.2.4 was installed and its status command exercised. Live API access
+stopped at Kaggle's authentication requirement: the setup session had no account
+credentials. No live kernel pull, GPU submission, training, or real result download
+has been verified. Complete the sign-in and daily workflow above on your computer
+before considering the remote workflow validated end-to-end.
